<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Mooring hardened-runtime entitlements (bundle.macOS.entitlements).
  Least privilege: no JIT, no unsigned executable memory, no library-validation bypass,
  no DYLD environment variables. WKWebView runs its JavaScript JIT in Apple's own
  WebContent process, so the app itself needs none of those exceptions.
  Not sandboxed (outside the Mac App Store), so outgoing SSH/RDP/VNC sockets need no
  network entitlement.

  Keychain (ADR-0006 optional OS-keyring wrap): the `keyring` crate uses the login keychain
  through the legacy SecItem API, which needs no entitlement. Restricting items to an access
  group requires a Developer ID signature with a team prefix; enable the block below only
  after the Apple Developer ID is configured (see docs/release.md), replacing TEAMID.

  <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
  <array>
    <string>TEAMID.xyz.homelab.mooring</string>
  </array>
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
